# Markdown standards and linting

All Markdown must follow standard Markdown (CommonMark + GitHub Flavored Markdown where applicable).

Before finalizing any Markdown file or substantial Markdown output:

1. Use valid heading hierarchy (do not skip levels).
2. Use fenced code blocks with language tags when code is present.
3. Keep lists, links, tables, and emphasis syntactically valid.
4. Run a Markdown linter (prefer markdownlint / markdownlint-cli2 when available) and fix reported issues before considering the work done.
5. If no linter is available in the environment, still apply markdownlint-style checks manually and note that automated lint was not run.

Do not leave broken links, unclosed fences, or inconsistent list markers in finalized Markdown.
